\description{
Season player stats of one team in one competition, one row per player.

Wraps \verb{GET https://s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/de.hokejovyzapis.cz/league-team-stats/\{season\}/\{league_id\}/\{team_id\}.json} of the DEL eSports bucket. Example: \url{https://s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com/de.hokejovyzapis.cz/league-team-stats/2026/1/12.json}.
Seasons are END years (2027 = 2026/27); every request waits at least one second after
the last one to the same host.
}
\section{Errors}{

Signalled as classed conditions: \code{fastRhockey_no_data} when the bucket has no such key (S3 404 NoSuchKey: unknown season, competition, match or team) or the file holds no rows (an unplayed game, an empty shot shell); \code{fastRhockey_asset_fetch} for any other non-2xx answer (403 AccessDenied), a connection failure after retries, an empty or unreadable 200 body, an error envelope, a body of the wrong shape, or a body for another season or game; \code{fastRhockey_bad_request} for an HTTP 400/422 or an invalid argument. All three also inherit \code{fastRhockey_error}. Wrappers raise; they never warn and return an empty frame.
}

